  "interpretation": [
    "Complete allocation/copy and distinct entire-body equality controls were small relative to separate full-client socket timings; these observations do not justify a buffer pool or unsafe initialization change.",
    "Final Linux four-thread medians were 0.962 ms allocation/copy, 0.344 ms exact equality, 17.754 ms independent complete Response clone, and 50.016 ms typed read. The typed-read p95 was 3512.666 ms; retain this outlier rather than infer a pure-load cause.",
    "Eight samples per case under shared development load are diagnostics, not a stable reference, live-reader pass, or proof acceptance.",
    "In-memory copying may compile differently from a Unix read. The raw transfer control includes a serial owned accept/write fixture, not the production daemon or a freshness observer. It parses and validates the entire response after timing.",
    "Separately timed components and client replays cannot be subtracted to identify residual live latency; no new production copy/clone optimization is claimed.",
    "Initial new raw-transfer diagnostic Clippy checks rejected 110-line and 102-line measure functions. Extracted helpers fixed them; final strict all-target check and three controls passed."
